#+TITLE: Cador rejects ssget crossing mode _C required by SCHMS occupancy tests
#+STATUS: DONE
#+PRIORITY: P1
#+TYPE: compatibility
#+DEPENDS: -
#+BRANCH: -
#+DATE: 2026-10-29

* Reproduction and scope

SCHMS+ branch =fix-pb-lisp-warnings= adds three native ActiveX regression
scenarios for =src-vlx/encombrement.lsp=,
=schms_chevauchement_encombrement_sauf=. They select actual drawing entities
with =ssget "_C"=, check exclusion of VLA objects and preservation of the
caller's =ename= binding. No CAD primitive is mocked.

The tests cannot execute this operation under clautolisp SBCL 2.3.73,
=--host cador --dialect bricscad-v26=. The installed Windows release 2.3.75
has the same selection dispatcher; current master 7411ff07 still rejects
all modes except X/_X/_I in =clautolisp/cador/source/selection-api.lisp=.
This is a missing host capability, not a regression attributed to a release.

Run the adjacent =ssget-crossing-selection-unsupported-repro.lsp= with:

#+begin_src sh
clautolisp --no-init --host cador --dialect bricscad-v26 \
  -l issues/closed/ssget-crossing-selection-unsupported-repro.lsp
#+end_src

Observed error:

#+begin_example
cador does not yet support ssget mode "_C"; accepted modes are "X", "_X" and "_I".
#+end_example

The fixture contains exactly two lines inside the crossing rectangle. A
supported implementation must return a selection containing both entities;
this reproducer prints PASS only after testing length and membership. It
cleans its own two entities on success and on the caught unsupported-mode
error. It needs no SCHMS installation or external DWG.

* Expected implementation and checks

Implement crossing selection with geometric intersection, including entities
crossing a boundary with neither endpoint inside; do not approximate it by
selecting all drawing entities. Test fully inside, crossing, outside, boundary,
empty selection, filters, and supported dialect/coordinate conventions.
Compare these semantics against native AutoCAD and BricsCAD before claiming
parity, especially view-dependent behaviour and UCS/WCS conversion.

SCHMS currently activates these three scenarios only in the actual native
CAD launchers, including the optimized DES/VLX qualification. Its existing
11 ActiveX tests still run in Cador; the output explicitly states the three
additional cases are outside that backend's current coverage. Once _C is
implemented, enable the same cases in the Cador lane and keep this minimal
reproducer in the implementation regression suite.

* Implemented -- 2026-11-16 (clautolisp 2.4.20)

(ssget "_C" P1 P2 [FILTER]) and (ssget "_W" P1 P2 [FILTER]) -- and the bare
"C" / "W" -- in cador (selection-api.lisp): the corners travel to the host as
HOST-SSGET's new :POINTS. Crossing = an entity with a point inside the
rectangle or crossing its boundary; window = entirely inside. Exact for LINE,
LWPOLYLINE (straight segments; a bulge taken as its chord), CIRCLE (the
curve: a circle enclosing the rectangle is NOT crossed), ARC (sampled), POINT;
the other kinds use the conservative bounding box. The rectangle is in the
WCS XY plane (cador has no view; its UCS is the WCS).

Checked: the adjacent repro prints PASS (clautolisp 2.4.20, --host cador
--dialect bricscad-v26); cador tests ssget-window-selects-entities-entirely-
inside, ssget-crossing-selects-inside-and-crossing-entities (a line through
the rectangle with no endpoint inside selected; an enclosing circle and a
square polyline around it not), ssget-crossing-applies-the-filter-and-may-
select-nothing, ssget-window-or-crossing-without-two-points-signals.

Native comparison: probes/sources/probe-ssget-window-crossing.lsp runs the
same geometry on AutoCAD and BricsCAD (this MR's probe:suite jobs). Close
once the three agree, or model what they show. Then enable the three SCHMS
encombrement scenarios in its cador lane.

* Native comparison -- 2026-11-16 (closed)

probe-ssget-window-crossing.lsp, captured by !553's probe:suite jobs:
AutoCAD 2022 Windows (job 18081159079, probe-results/autocad/ms-windows/
20261116T194606Z), BricsCAD Windows (18081159083, .../bricscad/ms-windows/
20261116T195029Z), BricsCAD macOS (18081159080, .../bricscad/macos/
20261116T194308Z).

BricsCAD on Windows AGREES WITH CADOR ON EVERY CASE -- window, crossing,
swapped corners, the LINE filter, the empty rectangle -- including the line
through the rectangle with no endpoint inside (selected) and the enclosing
circle and square polyline (not). The headless sessions are no witness:
AutoCAD's accoreconsole has no view and returns EVERY entity for every
window / crossing (the rectangle ignored, even with the LINE filter or an
empty rectangle); BricsCAD's macOS batch returns nil for all. The SCHMS
scenarios run under the bricscad-v26 dialect, whose product is the one that
agrees. Remaining outside this repository: enable the three encombrement
scenarios in SCHMS's cador lane.

